Sackar Atlas is a research project by Anna Roberts that makes the findings of the 2023 [Special Commission of Inquiry into LGBTIQ Hate Crimes](https://www.nsw.gov.au/departments-and-agencies/cabinet-office/resources/special-commissions-of-inquiry/lgbtiq-hate-crimes) navigable to a general audience.

Led by Justice John Sackar AO KC, the inquiry examined 30+ deaths in New South Wales between 1976 and 2000, many of which appeared to be LGBTIQ bias-motivated. The final report, running to over 3,000 pages, draws on earlier public records including the ACON [In Pursuit of Truth & Justice](https://www.aconhealth.org.au/report_into_historic_gay_hate_murders_calls_for_justice_and_healing) report and the [NSW Police Strike Force Parrabell](https://www.police.nsw.gov.au/safety_and_prevention/your_community/working_with_lgbtqia/strike_force_parrabell) findings.

This project structures those public findings as a cross-referenced dataset — cases, locations, people, events, and sources — with every claim geo-located and sourced to the primary record. The relationships between them are the argument. A PDF can't show them.

Designed for use by community organisations, journalists, researchers, and the general public. Open source and freely available. [Source code on GitHub](https://github.com/bitsloppy/sackar-atlas)
